 record on McMinn County&rsquo;s 7 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 years, the most of any pair. In 2025, November to December came in at 53% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 56% of normal and March to April at 60%, both on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
